<p>I'm so tired of every time an author decides to include a list, the last thing is <strong>always</strong> [EXPUNGED]. What are you trying to say? That you saved the most horrific thing for last, and it's so horrific that higher-ups removed it from the document? That you needed an even number of list items, but couldn't conjure up the final object? Is there a hidden rule that every article must [EXPUNGE] something? Someone needs to write an article explaining this before I try to.</p>

