<p>This was just a very boring idea to me. Reminds me way too much of Subtle Killer Morgan Freeman. The writing style and tone were top-notch though &#8212; Something that hasn't been seen here in a while. You then had to murder it with the final [EXPUNGED]. Why was that necessary? Cut out the expunged and put in pedophilia, I'm surprised that isn't on there as it is one of the most reputationally detrimental accusations and it is frequently inflicted on the innocent.</p>
<p>Also get rid of magic, because it exposes a plot hole that's present in another part of the article, but you can overlook the other one. I don't think that magic is something that one can be accused of in today's world. You have added that <em>somehow</em> the object has existed for thousands of years, yet there is no real way to prove that, but this would explain the magic idea better. However, if the item has only been under Foundation control since sometime in the 2000s, how would the Foundation be aware of effects of the item in medieval times, or at least when they had witch-hunts.</p>

